        body: 'Winning an IDIQ base contract. Like getting awarded a position on OASIS+. Is a significant achievement. It means the government has vetted you, qualified you, and put you in the pool of eligible vendors. But here\'s the honest truth: winning the base contract obligates almost nothing.\n\nThe base IDIQ sets the terms: the ordering period (how long agencies can place task orders), the ceiling value (the maximum total value of all task orders across all awardees), the labor categories and rate structures, and any vehicle-specific rules. But it doesn\'t direct specific work, and it doesn\'t obligate meaningful money. The minimum guarantee is often $1 per awardee, just enough to make the contract legally binding.\n\nWinning the base gets you on the team bus. It doesn\'t guarantee you\'ll play. Playing means winning task orders.',
