        body: 'If a TDL asks you to do something that wasn\'t in the SOW, adds funding, references extending the work beyond the current period of performance, or changes how the contract works. Stop. Do not start the work. Immediately notify the Contracting Officer in writing, explain the concern, and ask for a contract modification if the work is legitimate. Document the notification. This protects you legally and gives the government a chance to do the right paperwork.',
