            type: 'text',
            level: 'intermediate',
            heading: 'The Report and the Limitation of Funds Notice',
            body: 'The cost report is where the Limitation of Funds (or Limitation of Cost) obligation becomes visible. The clause requires the contractor to notify the CO in writing when it expects costs within a set period (often 60 days) to exceed a set percentage (often 75%) of the funded amount. The report\'s funds-exhausted date is the trigger. A contractor PM who sees the date inside the notice window and does not send the notice has forfeited the government\'s obligation to fund the overrun. A government PM who sees the same date and has not started the funding action has a stop-work coming. Both should be reading the same line.',
