            body: 'The catch-up reprices all the work you already did, not just this quarter\'s. If you were 50% complete at the old margin, half the lost profit was already sitting on the books and has to come back out now. Then the remaining work earns at the new, lower rate. So a mid-program EAC increase hits twice: once as a reversal of past profit, and again as lower profit on everything still to come.',
