            body: 'Many large contractors keep two estimates. The management EAC is the PM\'s most likely outcome, including planned risk mitigation and expected opportunities. The accounting EAC, used for revenue recognition, is typically more conservative: it includes identified risks at their expected value and excludes opportunities until they are highly probable. The difference is often held as a program-level reserve inside the EAC.\n\nSenior PMs need to speak both. In a program review, the management EAC drives decisions. In the quarterly close, the accounting EAC drives the numbers. Presenting the optimistic one to finance produces charges later. Presenting the conservative one to the customer invites questions about why you need so much money. Know which room you are in.',
