            body: 'Divide the bill rate by the employee\'s base hourly pay. Sarah at $95 per hour on a $48 base rate ($100K ÷ 2,080) is a 1.98 multiplier. Rules of thumb in defense services: below about 1.7 the company is almost certainly losing money at any realistic utilization; 1.8 to 2.1 is competitive and survivable at high utilization; above 2.2 is comfortable and usually only available on less competitive vehicles or highly specialized labor categories.\n\nThe multiplier is the fastest check a PM can do when asked to staff a labor category with a specific person. If the person\'s salary implies a multiplier below the company\'s floor, the answer is either a different person, a different labor category, or a conversation with pricing before the assignment is made.',
