            heading: 'Using the Filing Before a Teaming or Rate Negotiation',
            body: 'If you are about to negotiate with a prime, read its most recent 10-Q first. A segment under margin pressure will push subs on rates and workshare; a segment with favorable adjustments and rising backlog has room. If the filing names your program or one like it as a problem, expect scrutiny on every invoice. If contract assets are ballooning, expect slower payment terms. Twenty minutes of reading changes the tone of the negotiation, because you walk in knowing what the other side is measured on.',
