            body: 'Most defense contractors are private and file nothing public. But the same information exists internally and gets read by the same kinds of people. The bank\'s covenant package is the private version of the financial statements: trailing EBITDA, leverage ratio, fixed charge coverage. The board deck is the private MD&A: segment or contract results, backlog, pipeline, EAC adjustments. The quality of earnings report is what a buyer commissions to get the equivalent of an audited 10-K. A senior PM at a private contractor should ask to see the board deck\'s program pages and the backlog roll-forward; they are the company\'s own scorecard, and the PM\'s program is on it.',
