            body: 'Size is determined as of the date the company submits its initial offer including price. If the company is small on that date, it is small for that award, even if it grows past the standard before award or during performance. That rule is why a company at $45M against a $47M standard can still win a five-year contract as a small business: it was small when it bid.\n\nThe flip side: a company that is large on the day it bids cannot fix that by shrinking later, and a company that certifies small on the wrong date, or under the wrong NAICS, has made a false certification, which is a far bigger problem than losing the award.',
