            body: 'Every controlled item and every piece of technical data has a classification: a USML category under ITAR, or an ECCN under the EAR, or EAR99. That classification determines everything downstream. The manufacturer or developer is responsible for classifying its own products, using the order of review the regulations set out: check the USML first, then the CCL. When the answer is unclear, a company can request a commodity jurisdiction determination from DDTC or a classification from BIS. On a government program, the government often supplies the classification of the items and data it provides, but the contractor is responsible for what it generates. A PM should know the classification of the technical data on the program the way they know its CUI category, because the two usually go together.',
