            body: 'The rights category follows the money used to develop the item, component, or process. Developed exclusively at government expense means unlimited rights. Exclusively at private expense means limited or restricted. Mixed means government purpose rights. Two details make this workable and dangerous. First, "private expense" includes indirect costs like independent research and development that the government ultimately reimburses through overhead; IR&D-funded development is private expense. Second, the test is applied at the lowest practicable segregable level: a component developed privately can carry limited rights even inside a system developed with government money, if the contractor can show the funding for that component. That means a contractor\'s development accounting is its data rights evidence. If the company cannot show that a component was developed on IR&D rather than charged to a contract, it cannot assert limited rights in it.',
