            body: 'Federal employees may not accept gifts from prohibited sources, which includes anyone seeking business with or regulated by their agency. The main exception is small: items worth $20 or less per occasion, not exceeding $50 per year from any one source. Coffee, a modest meal at a widely attended gathering under specific conditions, promotional items of little value, and a few other categories are permitted. Anything beyond that is not, regardless of intent. Contractors who want to host government personnel at events, provide meals, or give holiday gifts need to know these limits, because the government employee who accepts an improper gift is the one who faces discipline, and the contractor that gave it is the one that faces the bribery and gratuities statutes if the gift can be connected to an official act. The safe practice: nothing of value beyond the exception, ever, and a written policy that says so.',
