              'Covenant against contingent fees|||Every contract includes the contractor\'s warranty that it did not pay anyone a fee contingent on winning, except a bona fide employee or a bona fide established commercial agency. Paying a consultant a success fee to "open doors" violates it, and the government can annul the contract or deduct the fee.',
