            body: 'For contracts over $6 million with a performance period over 120 days, FAR 52.203-13 requires a written code of business ethics and conduct within 30 days of award, given to every employee; an ongoing program of training and internal controls (unless the company is small, but do it anyway); a mechanism for employees to report concerns without retaliation, typically a hotline; periodic review of the program; disciplinary action for violations; and timely mandatory disclosure of credible evidence of specified violations. It also requires displaying the agency OIG fraud hotline poster. A small company can meet all of this with a ten-page code, an annual training session, an outside hotline service, and a compliance lead who reviews the program once a year. What it cannot do is skip it and hope the contract stays under the threshold.',
