            type: 'text',
            level: 'intermediate',
            heading: 'Protecting the Number',
            body: 'The IGCE is source selection information once the acquisition begins. It is not released to industry, it is marked and controlled, and disclosing it to an offeror is a Procurement Integrity Act violation. The people who build it should be the people who will evaluate against it, or their colleagues, and none of them should have a financial interest in any offeror. When contractors support the program office (advisory and assistance contractors are common), they must be walled off from the IGCE for any competition they or their affiliates might pursue, which is an OCI question the CO must address.',
