            body: 'For development work and novel requirements, a point estimate overstates what anyone knows. Senior estimators build ranges: a most-likely estimate with documented low and high cases driven by the major uncertainties (workload volume, technology maturity, staffing availability), and a risk-adjusted figure for the funding request. The Cost Estimating lesson in the Finance module covers cost risk calculation for programs; the same logic applies at IGCE scale. A funding request at the most-likely number with no reserve produces a contract that is underfunded the first time an assumption fails. The acquisition plan should say which figure is being funded and why.',
