            type: 'text',
            heading: 'Start With the Source Selection Plan',
            body: 'Before Section M is written, the government writes the source selection plan: who is on the evaluation team and in what roles (the SSA, an advisory council if used, the evaluation board and its technical, past performance, and price teams, the CO), what factors and subfactors will be evaluated and their relative importance, the rating scales and definitions, how price will be evaluated, whether discussions are planned, and the schedule. Section M is then written from the plan, and Section L is written so that proposals arrive in a form the plan can evaluate. Writing Section M first and the plan afterward produces evaluation methods the factors cannot support and page limits that do not match what the evaluators need.',
