            body: 'GAO sustains a minority of protests, and the sustained ones cluster around a few errors the solicitation and plan could have prevented. Unstated evaluation criteria: rewarding or penalizing something Section M did not identify. Unequal treatment: evaluating the same feature as a strength for one offeror and not another, or holding offerors to different standards. Inadequate documentation: an evaluation record that does not explain the ratings, or a source selection decision that does not explain the tradeoff. Mechanical tradeoffs: awarding to the higher-rated offer without explaining why the benefits were worth the price, or to the lower-priced without explaining why the other\'s advantages were not. Unreasonable evaluations: findings the record contradicts. Each of these is a discipline that begins with a clear Section M, a plan that trains evaluators to document findings against the stated criteria, and an SSA who writes the decision in comparative terms.',
