            body: 'The next two lessons cover each path in detail; here is the choice in one paragraph. The government civilian path offers stability, a pension that combines with military retirement under known rules, a mission continuity you will recognize, and a defined certification and grade ladder; it pays less at the top, hires slowly, and moves at the government\'s pace. The contractor path offers higher pay, faster hiring, more variety, and a direct connection between your work and the company\'s revenue; it carries billability pressure, contract-tied job security, and a customer who is not your employer. Many veterans do both over a career, and the crossing point is usually a clearance and a customer relationship. Decide based on what you want the next five years to feel like, not on which side sounds more familiar.',
