            body: 'The services\' transition assistance programs, the DoD SkillBridge program (which allows up to the last 180 days of service to be spent in an approved industry training or internship program while still on active duty, verify current rules), veteran employment programs run by nonprofits and large contractors, and the federal hiring preferences all exist for you. SkillBridge in particular is the best on-ramp available to the contractor side and increasingly to government offices: you work in the job before you leave service, the employer sees you perform, and the offer usually follows. Apply early, because the good SkillBridge positions fill months ahead. Treat every program as a door, not a guarantee; the work of translating and networking is still yours.',
