            body: 'Senior enlisted leaders and field-grade officers bring judgment, organizational skill, and a network that junior transitioners do not have, and acquisition organizations know it. They also have the most to unlearn. Acquisition rewards people who can build consensus among peers without authority, who can write a persuasive memorandum, who can wait a year for a decision without losing focus, and who can accept that the contracting officer, the tester, and the budget analyst each have a veto. A senior leader who tries to command a program office generates resistance without knowing why. The ones who thrive shift from directing to persuading in the first ninety days, ask more questions than they answer for six months, and use their judgment on what matters rather than on how things should be done.',
