            heading: 'The Acquisition Workforce Is Hiring, and It Is Hiring You',
            body: 'The DoD acquisition workforce is large, aging, and under a standing mandate to grow and renew. Contracting offices in particular have been short of qualified people for years. Veterans are the natural pipeline: the clearance, the customer knowledge, the preference in hiring, and the special authorities that let agencies bring you in without a full competition all point the same way. The obstacles are the ones every federal applicant faces (the announcement format, the HR screen, the slow timeline) plus the translation problem the previous lesson covered. This lesson is the mechanics: which jobs, which authorities, how the announcements work, and what the certification system will ask of you once you are in.',
